  "summary_text": "Kyle, Port Washington is running strong year-to-date\u2014up 39% on both revenue and appointments\u2014and that momentum carried into early October with a 24% MTD jump that beats calendar expectations by 3.4 points. Yesterday was softer (down 7% total, down 9% in grooming), but that's a capacity story: you ran six groomers at $452/groomer against a 30-day baseline of $487, and transaction count dropped 14%, suggesting appointment timing rather than team performance. The operational concern is add-on attach, which collapsed from 60% to 41%\u2014that's a upsell discipline issue worth a conversation with the floor. Retail held up nicely (+10%), so front-of-house focus isn't the problem there.\n\nHicksville is the story. Yesterday revenue jumped 31% on 53% more transactions, core grooms were up 45% week-over-week, and you're running +11.6% against DOW-adjusted expectations\u2014real outperformance. The friction: add-on attach fell from 40% to 12%, and retail cratered 45%. With zero bather hours scheduled and only 2.9 groomer-days per day MTD, you're resource-constrained in a way that's now visible in attach rate and retail conversion. That's not a problem; it's a signal you've found demand you can't yet fully serve.\n\nGlen Cove opened soft but is producing $265/groomer, and you have zero groomer-days scheduled for the next seven days. That's a staffing vacuum that needs immediate attention.\n\n**Capacity & coverage: Today Port Washington runs 7 groomers with 15.0h bathers; Hicksville 5 groomers, 0h bathers; Glen Cove dark; next 7 days Port 36 groomer-days, Hicksville 22, Glen Cove 0.**"
